{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.QuarkAntiquarkProduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.QuarkAntiquarkProduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QuarkAntiquarkProduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QuarkAntiquarkProduction","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.lean#L69-L77","doc":"Top-level Prop alias matching the manifest `lean.ref`\n`qou:QOU.Archimedean.QuarkAntiquarkProduction`: the residual-electron\ncoefficient of `L₊ · e⁻` is `h²` while the leading hadronic\ncoefficient is `1`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quark-antiquark-production","label":"def:quark-antiquark-production","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.quark_antiquark_production_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.quark_antiquark_production_witness","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.lean#L59-L67","doc":"Witness: the two cross-color Hopf channels `L₊` (from `φ₀ψ₁`) and\n`L₋` (from `φ₁ψ₀`) carry equal NF coefficient `h` in `L₊ · e⁻`,\nreflecting the chiral `quark/antiquark` symmetry of the two\nindependent pair productions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.quarkAntiquarkProduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.quarkAntiquarkProduction","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.lean#L40-L57","doc":"**Quark-antiquark production from Hopf-link pair creation.**\n\nThe Hopf link operator `L₊ = σ₀σ₁` acts as a quark creation\noperator: its action on the leptonic trefoil `e⁻` yields the\nnormal form `σ₁ + h L₊ + h L₋ + h² e⁻` (the dominant `σ₁` is the\nhadronic crossing, the residual `h² e⁻` is the surviving lepton\nfraction). This records the structural content of the manuscript\nderivation: the residual-electron coefficient is `h²` and the\nleading hadronic coefficient is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hopfTrefoilNFCoeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hopfTrefoilNFCoeffs","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.lean#L24-L38","doc":"**Normal-form coefficients of `L₊ · e⁻`** — the heart of the\nquark-creation computation in `def:quark-antiquark-production`.\n\nApplying the positive Hopf link `L₊ = σ₀σ₁` to the trefoil electron\n`e⁻ = σ₀σ₁σ₀` produces the five-letter word `σ₀σ₁σ₀σ₁σ₀`, which\nreduces in `H₃(q)` (braid relation + Hecke relation\n`σᵢ² = h σᵢ + 1`) to the normal form\n\n  `NF(L₊ · e⁻) = σ₁ + h·L₊ + h·L₋ + h²·e⁻`\n\nin the basis `{1, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻}`. The four nonzero\ncoefficients (over the standard NF basis) are therefore\n`(c_{σ₁}, c_{L₊}, c_{L₋}, c_{e⁻}) = (1, h, h, h²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heckeH","kind":"def","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/quark-antiquark-production.lean#L16-L22","doc":"Hecke-Skein quantum-integer differential `h(q) = q − q⁻¹`.\n\nBase ring (AGENTS.md §7c): a generic `[CommRing R]` with the modulus\ncarried as a **unit** `q : Rˣ`, so `↑q⁻¹` is a `Units` coercion — the\ndocstring's \"generic ring, `q` invertible\" made literal. No field,\nno ring inverse. ","signatureChunk":0}]}